This project is licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE).

It combines and builds on two open-source projects:

1. cloudera/NiFi-MCP-Server — https://github.com/cloudera/NiFi-MCP-Server
   (reference commit 9af7ce2930814e974d9c8b26330f7b2cb7431324)
   Copyright Cloudera, Inc. Licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
   Used as a functional reference for the tool catalogue and REST request shapes, and parts
   are adapted into this repository:
     - src/nifipilot_plus/guides/flow_builder.py   (copied, header added)
     - src/nifipilot_plus/guides/best_practices.py (modified)
     - src/nifipilot_plus/guides/jdbc.py           (extracted)
     - src/nifipilot_plus/client.py and src/nifipilot_plus/tools/* (re-implemented with
       httpx and optional revisions; request/response shapes follow the original)
   Changes are marked in the header of each adapted file, as required by Apache-2.0 §4(b).
   The Knox authentication layer of the original is intentionally NOT included.

2. Giojacke/mcp-nifipilot (NiFiPilot) — https://github.com/Giojacke/mcp-nifipilot
   (reference commit fd04b9730c4f57ccad2da4791b377d37388867e6)
   Declared as MIT in its README (see licenses/MIT-mcp-nifipilot.txt). The upstream repository
   did not contain a LICENSE file at that commit, so the copyright holder line is generic.
   Design ideas were taken from it: readonly/full mode, dry-run, audit log, NiFi login
   handling and HTTP/Docker deployment. To the best of our knowledge no source code or
   documentation text of it is included: the agent instructions (skills/nifi-operator.md)
   were originally adapted from its skill document and have since been rewritten from scratch.
   The MIT text is kept as an acknowledgment.

